  "finding": "Separate Stringer oriented-stimulus release contains six distinct named mice with running arrays referenced by the authors first-six-recording analysis. These identifiers differ from the seven MP identifiers in the already reviewed spontaneous release. This is a plausible additional validation cohort, not yet a validated replacement.",
  "limitations": [
    "The response files were not downloaded or inspected; response/running alignment and exact temporal aggregation remain unverified.",
    "Author analysis uses trial-indexed sresp and paired running arrays. Do not reinterpret trial indices as the original uniformly binned continuous activity without documenting timing.",
    "The current database has38records while all_running has32. Author notebook explicitly uses first6forrunning; later record mapping is not established.",
    "No target values, target distributions, decoding metrics, neuron eligibility or model choices were inspected on this cohort. Only identifiers, array shapes, dtypes and publisher hashes were checked.",
    "Stimulus-driven recordings change context from spontaneous behavior. Any future comparison needs a separately frozen protocol and equal preprocessing/controls.",
    "New identifiers suggest new animals; full provenance and non-overlap still require verification before an independent-animal claim."
  ],
